<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Feature Library — ERP Unite Learning Pack</title>
<style>
  :root { --navy: #00395F; --navy-dark: #00253D; --navy-light: #1A5A8A; --cyan: #079FC3; --cyan-light: #4AB9D4; --teal: #00B294; --red: #F1554B; --yellow: #F2B949; --slate: #44546A; --mute: #737373; --bg: #FAFBFC; --border: #E5E9EE; }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', sans-serif; color: var(--navy); background: var(--bg); line-height: 1.6; }
  .hero { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--navy-dark) 0%, var(--navy) 50%, var(--navy-light) 100%); color: white; padding: 64px 40px 84px; position: relative; }
  .hero::after { content: ''; position: absolute; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 4px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--cyan) 0%, var(--teal) 50%, var(--cyan) 100%); }
  .hero-inner { max-width: 1300px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .breadcrumb { color: var(--cyan-light); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 1.5px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .breadcrumb a { color: var(--cyan-light); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px dotted rgba(74, 185, 212, 0.5); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 60px; font-weight: 300; letter-spacing: -1px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .hero h1 strong { font-weight: 600; color: var(--cyan-light); }
  .hero p { font-size: 20px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82); max-width: 760px; }
  main { max-width: 1300px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 60px 40px 80px; }
  .group-label { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--cyan); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-top: 48px; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; }
  .group-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .group-label .count { color: var(--mute); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; }
  .feat-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(360px, 1fr)); gap: 18px; }
  .feat-card { background: white; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 26px; text-decoration: none; color: inherit; transition: transform 0.18s ease, box-shadow 0.18s ease, border-color 0.18s ease; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; min-height: 160px; }
  .feat-card:hover { transform: translateY(-3px); box-shadow: 0 12px 28px rgba(0, 57, 95, 0.14); border-color: var(--cyan); }
  .feat-card .num { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--cyan); letter-spacing: 1.5px; }
  .feat-card h3 { font-size: 19px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin: 4px 0 6px 0; }
  .feat-card p { font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--slate); line-height: 1.55; }
  .feat-card .open-cue { margin-top: auto; padding-top: 12px; color: var(--cyan); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; }
  footer { background: var(--navy-dark); color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7); padding: 24px 40px; text-align: center; font-size: 13px; }
  footer a { color: var(--cyan-light); text-decoration: none; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .hero h1 { font-size: 40px; } .feat-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="hero">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="index.html">← ERP Unite Learning Pack</a></div>
    <h1>Feature <strong>Library</strong></h1>
    <p>Every business capability of ERP Unite, organized by hub. Click any feature for what it does, the problem it solves, what the user does day-to-day, the key screens, and the business value — with technical anchors collapsed for the developers who need them.</p>
    <p style="margin-top: 18px; color: var(--cyan-light); font-size: 15px;">→ Read straight through with Next-Next-Next, or jump to any feature directly.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
<div class="group-label"><span>Cash Hub</span><span class="count">9 features</span></div><div class="feat-grid"><a class="feat-card" href="feature-statement-intake.html">
  <span class="num">01</span>
  <h3>Statement Intake & Bulk Import</h3>
  <p>Receive every carrier statement, fingerprint it, queue it for processing — single file or hundreds at once.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-mapping-studio.html">
  <span class="num">02</span>
  <h3>Mapping Studio (AI Template Authoring)</h3>
  <p>Google Gemini proposes how each carrier's statement maps to canonical fields. A human reviewer approves. New format onboarded in minutes.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-statement-detail-workflow.html">
  <span class="num">03</span>
  <h3>Statement Detail Workflow (the 6-Tab Deep Dive)</h3>
  <p>Every statement opens into a tabbed work surface: Dashboard / Lines (Original) / Lines / Statement Review / Unmatched / Review & Approve.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-cash-app-matching.html">
  <span class="num">04</span>
  <h3>Cash Application Matching (Auto + Learning Rules)</h3>
  <p>Auto-match cash app lines to products and customers. Every manual fix becomes a learning rule that catches the same pattern next time.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-research-cases.html">
  <span class="num">05</span>
  <h3>Research Cases</h3>
  <p>Investigation tracker for cash app lines that resist even manual matching. Assigned, aged, audit-trailed.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-cash-deposits-matching.html">
  <span class="num">06</span>
  <h3>Cash Deposits & Statement ↔ Cash Matching</h3>
  <p>Bank-feed deposits matched to the statements that explain them. The last reconciliation step before downstream cash app can run cleanly.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-ah-journals.html">
  <span class="num">07</span>
  <h3>AH Journals & Manual Journal Batches</h3>
  <p>The four-eye control for everything that posts to the General Ledger.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-accruals-workflow.html">
  <span class="num">08</span>
  <h3>Accruals Workflow</h3>
  <p>Month-end accruals from preview through approval to AH journal. Workflow-controlled, audit-trailed, configurable per cost center.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-collections-cases.html">
  <span class="num">09</span>
  <h3>Collections Cases (Aged Accrual Write-Offs)</h3>
  <p>Non-invoiced collections worklist. Aged accruals get a case, an owner, an investigation trail, and (eventually) a generated write-off journal.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a></div><div class="group-label"><span>Compensation Hub</span><span class="count">7 features</span></div><div class="feat-grid"><a class="feat-card" href="feature-comp-actuals.html">
  <span class="num">10</span>
  <h3>Compensation Actuals (Producer Pay)</h3>
  <p>The system of record for producer pay. Batches, adjustments, invoice IDs on approval, bidirectional with AH.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-split-intake.html">
  <span class="num">11</span>
  <h3>Split Intake (SIF) Workflow</h3>
  <p>Multi-producer commission splits per opportunity. Versioned, audit-trailed, workflow-approved, with hierarchy-aware permissions.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-sif-rates-management.html">
  <span class="num">12</span>
  <h3>SIF Rates Management (Bulk + Audit + Coverage)</h3>
  <p>Power-user surfaces for rate-table operations: bulk rate updates, full audit log, coverage gap detection.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-producer-comp-rules.html">
  <span class="num">13</span>
  <h3>Producer Comp Rules (VCP Rate Table)</h3>
  <p>The base rate table per producer × vertical × renewal year. The numbers that drive every compensation calc.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-parties-producers.html">
  <span class="num">14</span>
  <h3>Parties & Producers Management</h3>
  <p>The people directory. Every internal staff member, every external producer, every external user — one master record per person.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-external-users.html">
  <span class="num">15</span>
  <h3>External Users (Invite + Entra)</h3>
  <p>Invite non-HSO partners (brokers, producers, agencies) into the Producer Portal via Microsoft Entra External ID.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-user-security.html">
  <span class="num">16</span>
  <h3>User Security (Roles, Permissions, Hierarchy)</h3>
  <p>Define roles. Assign permissions to roles. Assign roles to users with optional hierarchy scoping.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a></div><div class="group-label"><span>Producer Portal</span><span class="count">2 features</span></div><div class="feat-grid"><a class="feat-card" href="feature-portal-sales-intake.html">
  <span class="num">17</span>
  <h3>Portal Sales Intake (Producer Self-Service)</h3>
  <p>Producers submit and track their own splits. Same SIF data as the admin side, scoped to the producer's book.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-portal-authentication.html">
  <span class="num">18</span>
  <h3>Portal Authentication (Dual-OIDC)</h3>
  <p>Two identity providers, one Blazor app. Internal staff and external partners coexist in the same portal.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a></div><div class="group-label"><span>Integration Hub</span><span class="count">4 features</span></div><div class="feat-grid"><a class="feat-card" href="feature-ah-data-sync.html">
  <span class="num">19</span>
  <h3>Accounting Hub DataSync (14-Handoff Bridge)</h3>
  <p>The master integration bridge between Unite and OneDigital's Accounting Hub. 14 handoff/polling pairs covering every transaction class.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-cashhub-automation.html">
  <span class="num">20</span>
  <h3>CashHub Automation (Internal Batch Processing)</h3>
  <p>Nightly accrual processing, auto-cash-matching, statement bulk import, mapping enrichment — the unattended back-office.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-masterdata-integrations.html">
  <span class="num">21</span>
  <h3>MasterData Integrations (Mulesoft → Products & Customers)</h3>
  <p>Inbound master data from Mulesoft. Durable orchestration enriches products before they're available to downstream features.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-common-integrations.html">
  <span class="num">22</span>
  <h3>Common Integrations (FinOps Bridge + Reference Data)</h3>
  <p>AH↔FinOps bridges, vendor/employee sync, fiscal periods, financial dimensions, Databricks queries, reference data seeding.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a></div><div class="group-label"><span>Cross-cutting</span><span class="count">3 features</span></div><div class="feat-grid"><a class="feat-card" href="feature-authorization-framework.html">
  <span class="num">23</span>
  <h3>Authorization Framework</h3>
  <p>Permission-based RBAC with Global / Regional / Hierarchy scopes. The substrate every feature gates on.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-workflow-framework.html">
  <span class="num">24</span>
  <h3>Workflow Framework</h3>
  <p>Generic state-machine pattern with hooks. Every business-workflow surface (SIF, accruals, comp batches, collections) uses it.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a><a class="feat-card" href="feature-ai-services.html">
  <span class="num">25</span>
  <h3>AI Services (Gemini + Trace)</h3>
  <p>Shared AI inference layer with audit trace. Powers Mapping Studio and MasterData enrichment; replaceable if needed.</p>
  <span class="open-cue">Open feature guide →</span>
</a></div>
</main>

<footer>
  Part of the <a href="index.html">ERP Unite Learning Pack</a> · 25 features · also see the <a href="screens-library.html">Screens library</a>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
